# Example environment file for setup-neuron-dlc.sh.
#
# You do NOT need this file to use the public AWS Neuron DLC.
# Running `bash scripts/setup-neuron-dlc.sh pull` with no environment
# set will pull the default public image documented in the script.
#
# Only copy this template if you want to override the defaults, for
# example to pin a different tag or point at a private image:
#
#   cp setup/single-node/docs/dlc.env.example ~/.config/neuron-dlc.env
#   $EDITOR ~/.config/neuron-dlc.env
#   set -a; source ~/.config/neuron-dlc.env; set +a
#   bash setup/single-node/scripts/setup-neuron-dlc.sh venv
#
# Keep your actual environment file outside the repository tree (or at a
# path ignored by .gitignore) so that image identifiers are not committed.

# --- Override a single component of the public default ---

# ECR account hosting the image.
# Default: 763104351884 (public AWS Neuron DLC account).
# NEURON_DLC_ACCOUNT=

# ECR repository name.
# Default: pytorch-training-neuronx. Alternatives include
# pytorch-inference-neuronx.
# NEURON_DLC_REPO=

# ECR image tag. Verify against
# https://github.com/aws-neuron/deep-learning-containers/releases
# before pinning a new version.
# NEURON_DLC_TAG=

# --- OR specify a complete URI that bypasses the composition above ---

# Full ECR image URI including tag. Takes precedence over the individual
# NEURON_DLC_{ACCOUNT,REPO,TAG,REGION} values above when set.
#   <aws-account-id>.dkr.ecr.<region>.amazonaws.com/<repo>:<tag>
# NEURON_DLC_IMAGE_URI=

# Optional. Defaults to the region resolved from IMDSv2 (falling back to
# AWS_REGION, then us-west-2).
# NEURON_DLC_REGION=us-west-2

# Optional. Where the script extracts /workspace from the image.
# NEURON_DLC_WORKSPACE_DIR=$HOME/neuron-dlc-workspace

# Optional. Where the script creates a Python venv.
# NEURON_DLC_VENV_DIR=$HOME/neuron-dlc-venv

# Optional. Python interpreter used to build the venv.
# NEURON_DLC_VENV_PYTHON=python3

# Optional. Colon-separated list of globs (relative to the extracted
# workspace) to `pip install`. Examples:
#   NEURON_DLC_WHEEL_GLOBS="wheels/*.whl"
#   NEURON_DLC_WHEEL_GLOBS="wheels-a/*.whl:wheels-b/*.whl:editable-pkg-c"
# NEURON_DLC_WHEEL_GLOBS=

# Optional. Subdir of the extracted workspace that holds on-host .deb
# packages for the `runtime` mode.
# NEURON_DLC_RUNTIME_DEB_DIR=runtime_artifacts
